-- ====================================================]] function HTMLHelp07()
    DialogWindow.Help07 = [[<head><title>Help</title></head> ]] .. Style7() .. [[
    <body>
    <div class="layout">
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Definitions</label></div>
        <p class="h1-help">This page defines these items:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Dado Height</li>
          <li>Bottom panel connection</li>
          <li>Dog Bone joint</li>
          <li>T-Bone joint</li>
          <li>Sniglet joint</li>
          <li>Through joint</li>
          <li>Blind joint</li>
        </ul>
        <div><hr /></div>
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Dado Height</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/MillHeight02.png"  alt="Dado Height" width="550"></div>
        <p class="h1-help">Dado Height is the thickness of the material that stays under a dado. It is dimension A, B
        or C in the image. It is not the depth of the dado (dimension X, Y or Z).</p>
        <p class="h1-help">The gadget cuts each dado to a depth of panel thickness minus Dado Height.</p>
        <p class="h1-help" style="background-color: #FFF4CE; border: 1px solid #D9A400; padding: 6px 8px;">
        <strong>CAUTION:</strong> Do not enter a dado depth in the Dado Height field. If you do, the dadoes are at the
        wrong depth, and the drawer is not the correct size.</p>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Bottom Panel Connection</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/BottomJoints02.png" alt="Bottom Styles" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help">
          <p>The image shows three types of bottom connection. The gadget makes only item 2, the captured
          connection.</p>
          <ul class="box">
            <li><strong>Item 1:</strong> Rabbeted connection.</li>
            <li><strong>Item 2:</strong> Captured connection. The bottom panel is in a dado in the side, front and back
                panels.</li>
            <li><strong>Item 3:</strong> On-top connection.</li>
            <li><strong>Dimension A:</strong> The Dado Height.</li>
            <li><strong>Dimension B:</strong> The depth of the bottom panel in the dado.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Dog Bone Joint</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/DogBone.png"  alt="Dog Bone Joint" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help"><p>A round bit cannot cut a square inside corner. A relief cut removes the material in
        the corner, so the mating finger can go fully into the notch. The Dog Bone joint has its relief cut at 45
        degrees into each inside corner. It removes the least material of the three relief styles.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>T-Bone Joint</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/T-Bone.png"  alt="T-Bone Joint" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help"><p>The T-Bone joint has its relief cut at 90 degrees, along the bottom of the notch. Thus,
        the face of the mating finger touches a flat surface for the glue.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Sniglet Joint</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/Singlet.png"  alt="Sniglet Joint" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help"><p>The Sniglet joint is like the T-Bone joint, but its relief cut has a curved entry into
        the material. The curve decreases the sudden change of direction of the bit.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Through Joint</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/Through.png"  alt="Through Joint" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help"><p>In a through joint, the end grain of the fingers shows on the outside of both
        panels.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div class="helpframe">
        <div class="h3-lP"><label>Blind Joint</label></div>
        <div class="helpimages"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/Blind.png"  alt="Blind Joint" width="500"></div>
        <div class="h1-help"><p>Each relief style has a blind version. In a blind joint, the gadget keeps a thin layer
        of material on the panel. This layer covers the end grain of the mating fingers, so the joint is almost
        invisible. Blind Tab Thickness on the Milling menu sets the thickness of this layer.</p></div>
      </div>
        <div><hr /></div>
      <span class="helpimagesFooter"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[/Help/Images/Footer.png" width="80" height="20" alt="Page Footer"></span>
      </div>
        <div class="foot" id="FooterBox">
      <div><hr /></div>
      <div align="center">
        <input id="ButtonOK" class="FormButton" name="ButtonOK" type="button" value="Close"  />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>]]
    return true
end -- function end
-- ====================================================]]
